    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-331954",
      "knowledge_point_id": "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-{45}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=b+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{72}^{∘}).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-{45}^{∘} & ={30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 5x-{45}^{∘} & ={150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & ={30}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={150}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={75}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 5x & ={195}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={39}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b={39}^{∘}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
