      "math_academy_id": "q-274647",
      "knowledge_point_id": "fc8166bb-3a9d-5808-af53-a18ca99920f8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Sine Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=\\pi +2\\pi n,\\,x=b\\pi +2\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $b$ in the range $[0,2).$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{6\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\pi +2\\pi n & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
