      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=1\n$$\n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as \n\n$$\nx=\\pi a+\\pi n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Which of the following could be the value of $a?$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4} & =0+2\\pi n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\frac{3}{8}.$",
