      "math_academy_id": "q-328240",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+{50}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=a+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $({0}^{∘},{90}^{∘}].$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+{50}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & x+{50}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={135}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={225}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={85}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={85}^{∘}.$",
