      "knowledge_point_id": "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function",
      "problem": "Consider the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{125}^{∘})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe general solution of this equation can be expressed as\n\n$$\nx=-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\\,x=a+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is any integer. Find a possible value of $a$ in the range $[{0}^{∘},{180}^{∘}).$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+{125}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n, & \\, & \\, & 2x+{125}^{∘} & ={315}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={315}^{∘}-{125}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 2x & =-{80}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={190}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & =-{40}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n & \\, & \\, & x & ={95}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that $a={95}^{∘}.$",
