      "problem": "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation: \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(4x-90^\\circ\\right)} = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n, & \\, & \\, & 4x-{90}^{∘} & =-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={90}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & ={90}^{∘}-{150}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ 4x & ={60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & 4x & =-{60}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}n \\\\ x & ={15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n & \\, & \\, & x & =-{15}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
      "missing_source_fields": [
