    {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8659",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a180dc90-c6b9-577e-9eef-ed60ecafe4e5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution to an Equation Containing a Transformed Cosine Function",
      "problem": "Find the general solution of the following trigonometric equation:\n\n$$\n\\cos \\left(6x + 75^\\circ \\right) = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+{75}^{∘} & ={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 6x+{75}^{∘} & ={225}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 6x & ={150}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={25}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "difficulty": null,
